# Bridge ABI & syscalls

- Bridge C ABI + frontend binds with plain `declare xl_<object>_<action>(...)` (e.g. `xl_thread_start`). Never `declare syscall` for bridges.
- `declare syscall <number> name(...)` = CPU-native trap wrapper. `@syscall(num, args...)` = inline trap.
- Compiler: blind `declare`/`call` for bridges — no whitelist, no `needs_*_link` from name analysis.
- OS APIs live in `src/runtime/bridge/{linux,macosx,windows}/`; codegen has no PlatformIrBuilder.
- Link: OS baseline syslibs + embedded/override runtime/bridges. Prefer static embed into user programs.
